From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:01:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 150/207] Add checked 256-digit arithmetic graph templates

Extend optional graph banks with 256-digit add, subtraction, multiplication and power schedules while preserving old weights and lazy loading. Reuse temporary registers to fit the offline circuit memory budget.

Add boundary, mutation and integration proof fixtures. Finalize completed packs without rebuilding weights, retaining the original compiler provenance.

(cherry picked from commit b047d48c8dc704c871f6056800839e657b5d3ff9)
